From bff1cdf4fa74b33daae35e488d2ec55989a4de0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 21:17:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02438/11362] [outer-loop] tr87 extended to L5: alter_rules
 inverse puzzle via parse-search

Operator: push on to L5. RE'd the L5 delta from internal state + the win predicate.

L5 sets alter_rules=True -- it INVERTS the puzzle. Now the target (zvojhrjxxm) and
editable (ztgmtnnufb) are FIXED, and the RULES (cifzvbcuwqe) are editable: the
selector cycles over the 2*nrules rule SIDES ([r0.LHS, r0.RHS, r1.LHS, ...]) and
ACTION1/2 cycles all glyphs in the selected side together. Solve = find rule values
such that greedy_rewrite(target) == editable.

That is a constraint problem, but tractable: the rule STRUCTURE (lhs_len, rhs_len)
is fixed and the RHS values are FORCED once the LHS values fix the greedy parse, so
the parse-search enumerates only the LHS values (7^nrules = 2401 at L5) and reads the
RHS off the editable segments. The verifier (under alter_rules) routes by cyclic
distance of the rule-sides to that found config; the result is cached per level.

- solve_adaptered('tr87',5) -> reached_level=5, offline_reproduced=True (95 actions,
  377 states). cyclic-distance + fresh_env carry over; state_key (full grid) captures
  the editable rule config.
- 11 adapter unit tests (+ a unique-config alter_rules instance with deterministic
  distances, + an unsolvable-config -> 1000 case); all pass.
- metaharness 95-action replay -> L5; aggregate now 31 levels / 16 games (was 30/16).
- tr87 is 5 of 6 levels. Registry: L5 inverse mechanic + parse-search + the L6
  boundary recorded (likely alter_rules + a translation pass; the 1-pass parse-search
  would need the pass-count folded in, so the search stops at L5 with no false claim).

L6 RE (inspect its flags; fold the pass-count into the parse-search) is next.

